  "live_records": {
    "q-74856": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74856",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191212/assets/dbc4368e30cfd0543d085fc8baa644031b35f4086f2da53d5aaecf6b4b626245.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $∠B$ in the triangle  $△ABC$ above?",
      "worked_solution": "Since two sides are congruent, $\\overset{―}{AC}≅\\overset{―}{CB},$ we conclude that $△ABC$ is isosceles. Consequently, the base angles must have the same measure:\n\n$$\nm∠A=m∠B=2x-{9}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNow, since the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ (2x-{9}^{∘})+(2x-{9}^{∘})+(4x+{14}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 8x-{4}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={184}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={23}^{∘}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x={23}^{∘}$ into the equation for the measure of $∠B$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠B & =m∠A \\\\  & =2x-{9}^{∘} \\\\  & =2({23}^{∘})-{9}^{∘} \\\\  & ={37}^{∘}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $m∠B={37}^{∘}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
