    "q-118661": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118661",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191212/assets/4da332c74f255825ae0073ca41117ae477f72262ef8d45911b9ce48ed3b8ccf0.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $∠G$ in the triangle $△FGH$ above?",
      "worked_solution": "Since two sides are congruent, $\\overset{―}{FG}≅\\overset{―}{GH},$ we conclude that $△FGH$ is isosceles. Consequently, the base angles must have the same measure:\n\n$$\nm∠F=m∠H=x+{13}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNow, since the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠F+m∠G+m∠H & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ (x+{13}^{∘})+(2x+{18}^{∘})+(x+{13}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x+{44}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={136}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={34}^{∘}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x={34}^{∘}$ into the equation for the measure of $∠G$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠G & =2x+{18}^{∘} \\\\  & =2({34}^{∘})+{18}^{∘} \\\\  & ={86}^{∘}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $m∠G={86}^{∘}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
