    "q-118675": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118675",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191212/assets/e4600221042deaad471de628179200fa62872fdfe38220ca66eaded966f8894e.png)\n\nFind the value of $w$ in the triangle shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "First, from the diagram, notice that $∠RTS$ and $∠STU$ are supplementary. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠RTS+m∠STU & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RTS+w & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠RTS & ={180}^{∘}-w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $△RST$ is an isosceles triangle where $\\overset{―}{RT}≅\\overset{―}{TS}$, the base angles must be equal:\n\n$$\nm∠S=m∠R={39}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the interior angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠R+m∠S+m∠RTS & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {39}^{∘}+{39}^{∘}+({180}^{∘}-w) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {39}^{∘}+{39}^{∘}-w & =0 \\\\ w & ={78}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
