      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191212/assets/c182b73af6ff37c3c673fe0e174e8f86e2f89a0d38ed385f64e8b8b3a4731fc8.png)\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ shown above is isosceles with base $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ What is the measure of $\\overset{―}{BC}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle with base $\\overset{―}{BC}$, we have that $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =AC \\\\ 3x-3 & =2x+2 \\\\ x & =5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this value into the expression for the measure of $\\overset{―}{BC}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x-4 \\\\  & =2(5)-4 \\\\  & =6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
