    "q-118950": {
      "dom_id": "step-q118950",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191212/assets/dcd036443bb904abafd7ad0cc2aea6ead68538835c08d8b99958291f393a4476.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $∠S$ above?",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that $△PQR$ is an equilateral triangle. Consequently, all of the interior angles must be equal to ${60}^{∘}:$ \n\n$$\nm∠P=m∠PQR=m∠QRP={60}^{∘}\n$$\n\nAlso, since $△QRS$ is an isosceles triangle, the base angles must have equal measure:\n\n$$\nm∠RQS=m∠S\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191212/assets/792155c685456f6c278fff5a0341f67358a8b0983d696cf55a6867c9c71ec7cb.png)\n\nNotice also that $∠QRP$, $∠SRQ$ and $∠TRS$ are supplementary, therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠QRP+m∠SRQ+m∠TRS & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {60}^{∘}+m∠SRQ+{70}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠SRQ+{130}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠SRQ & ={50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in $△QRS$, using the fact that the interior angles of a triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠RQS+m∠S+m∠SRQ & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠S+m∠S+{50}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠S & ={130}^{∘} \\\\ m∠S & ={65}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
